lzz test suite
==============

probes/          one tiny .lzz file per language feature; t01..t20
expected.txt     expected PASS/FAIL per probe for the current lzz
run_probes.sh    run probes against a binary, compare with expected.txt
run_corpus.sh    regenerate a production corpus (default: sdt at
                 /z6pool/z/work/zmed3/sdt/src) with a candidate binary and
                 byte-compare .h/.cpp output against a reference binary

Workflow for a feature patch:
  1. implement the feature
  2. flip the relevant FAIL -> PASS in expected.txt (same commit)
  3. ./run_probes.sh <new-binary>        -> must report all-match
  4. ./run_corpus.sh <new-binary>        -> must report corpus clean
     (the corpus uses none of the new syntax yet, so output must be
     byte-identical for everything the patch did not touch)
  5. self-host: rebuild lzz with the new binary; generated code must be
     identical and the result must pass 3 and 4 again

Building: just type `make` at the repo root (drives tools/build.sh; builds
the static binary as bin/lzz-`uname -m` and runs the probes).  `make install`
copies bin/* verbatim to /usr/local/bin (a dispatcher script plus one static
binary per architecture).  `make cleanall && make install` is the
fresh-install-on-any-machine recipe; bin/ is never cleaned.  The corpus
baseline (and bootstrap of last resort) is the frozen pre-modernization
binary in /z6pool/z/dev/lzz/bin.OLD.  The notes below document what build.sh
does and why:
  - bootstrap needs an lzz binary; the frozen pre-modernization binary in
    /z6pool/z/dev/lzz/bin.OLD is preferred (deterministic, tomc keeps it),
    falling back to an installed lzz or a previous bin/ binary for clones
    outside this tree (override with LZZ=...)
  - BUILD ON LOCAL DISK.  Building inside an NFS-mounted tree (especially a
    soft mount) intermittently produces empty .o files: the compiler can read
    a just-generated .cpp before its data is visible.  Set CONFIGDIR (and
    OBJDIR/BUILD_LZZ) to a /tmp path:
        cd <repo>; source setup_gcc_opt.env
        export CONFIGDIR=/tmp/lzz-build/gcc.opt
        export OBJDIR=$CONFIGDIR/objs BUILD_LZZ=$CONFIGDIR/lzz
        mkdir -p $CONFIGDIR/gencode $CONFIGDIR/objs $CONFIGDIR/libs
        make gencode && make
    (run `make gencode` first: the per-directory loop compiles each subdir
    right after generating it, but sources include headers generated by
    later subdirs; the loop also ignores subdir failures)
  - do not use -j: parallel ar invocations corrupt the static libs
  - after regenerating parser tables (test/run_gate.sh --update), do a CLEAN
    rebuild (rm -rf $CONFIGDIR).  gram_Nonterm.lzz renumbers its accept
    handlers when rules change; incrementally-rebuilt objects that still hold
    the old numbering dispatch nodes to the wrong visitors (symptom: bizarre
    parse errors on valid input, core dumps)
